WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:03.420
<i>I was happy
to give Don Wei a hand</i>

00:03.710 --> 00:05.300
<i>and coach
the Earth team for a while.</i>

00:06.130 --> 00:07.720
<i>There are things, however,</i>

00:08.050 --> 00:10.340
<i>that even the best coach
can't foresee.</i>

00:10.840 --> 00:12.350
Stop hurting yourself.

00:12.510 --> 00:14.260
This is not what your mother
would have wanted.

00:14.770 --> 00:17.730
<i>It turns out Molly
is Don Wei's daughter, Eva.</i>

00:18.190 --> 00:20.060
Though she's keeping it a secret.

00:20.600 --> 00:23.690
<i>I hope you find the strength to face
your inner demons, little mouse.</i>

00:25.690 --> 00:28.240
<i>The great race may prove
a greater challenge</i>

00:28.400 --> 00:30.490
<i>than any of us ever imagined.</i>

01:40.560 --> 01:42.100
<i>Come on, Rick.</i>

01:42.270 --> 01:44.560
<i>The team's almost there.</i>

01:50.320 --> 01:52.070
Hey, what's this?

02:05.670 --> 02:08.000
Add two welding ports
to that flap over there.

02:08.460 --> 02:10.090
We're OK here.
Check the other side.

02:42.700 --> 02:44.920
You're not repairing
the Whizzing Arrow.

02:45.080 --> 02:46.330
You're building a new one!

02:47.000 --> 02:49.750
We designed these upgrades
when we were still working at Miguel's.

02:50.550 --> 02:51.800
And then we forgot about them.

02:53.050 --> 02:55.300
If we had known
about these Scrub mechanics,

02:55.470 --> 02:57.180
we would have done it
right away.

02:57.800 --> 02:59.100
You had better be right.

02:59.260 --> 03:03.140
Our last chance to qualify for Oban
starts in just a few hours.

03:08.940 --> 03:11.980
Hey, Stan, did you remember
to check the internal cooling system?

03:16.700 --> 03:19.530
Hello, there.
Quite a party you're having.

03:19.990 --> 03:21.280
You have something to tell me?

03:21.700 --> 03:23.120
What do you mean?

03:25.660 --> 03:28.290
Ah, oh, yes, of course.

03:28.580 --> 03:29.960
Silly me.

03:30.210 --> 03:33.420
The judges have finished
drawing lots for the final race.

03:34.130 --> 03:35.260
Drawing lots?

03:35.420 --> 03:39.300
The six teams in the playoffs
have already faced each other once.

03:39.470 --> 03:43.220
For the sixth race,
the opponents are picked at random.

03:43.890 --> 03:44.560
I see.

03:44.930 --> 03:48.060
It's all in that document,
the names of the opponents,

03:48.230 --> 03:51.860
the rules in case of a tie,
the departure tables for Oban,

03:52.020 --> 03:53.730
or in case of a defeat,

03:54.190 --> 03:57.240
the return trip
to your home planet.

04:15.710 --> 04:17.130
Isn't she beautiful?

04:17.840 --> 04:21.850
Stronger, faster, safer.

04:22.970 --> 04:25.270
The Whizzing Arrow 3.

04:29.140 --> 04:30.350
Brand new ship...

04:31.100 --> 04:33.230
for a brand new champion.

04:34.110 --> 04:35.280
Thanks a lot, guys.

04:35.440 --> 04:36.650
It's wonderful work.

04:36.820 --> 04:38.450
We couldn't have done it
without you.

04:48.080 --> 04:49.960
Well, sir, what's the verdict?

04:50.210 --> 04:51.750
Yeah, looks great.

04:53.170 --> 04:55.800
I have the name
of our next adversary.

04:56.460 --> 04:58.170
We're up against Colonel Toros.

04:58.800 --> 05:01.640
But he's never lost
a race. Ever.

05:02.390 --> 05:05.260
And he nearly crushed us
to a pancake last time.

05:05.810 --> 05:09.270
This team has improved tremendously
since we lost to Toros.

05:11.310 --> 05:13.730
Fill the tanks and run
the final checks right now.

05:14.230 --> 05:16.230
We'll be called
at any moment now.

05:16.400 --> 05:18.190
Yes, sir. We're on it!

05:18.820 --> 05:21.490
Uh, after you, partner.

05:37.500 --> 05:40.340
Remember, to rank
among the top three teams

05:40.510 --> 05:44.970
and qualify for Oban,
we must beat Toros at all costs.

05:45.430 --> 05:47.310
<i>Torus or no Toms,</i>

05:47.470 --> 05:50.640
no one stands between
the Ultimate Prize and me,

05:50.810 --> 05:52.140
<i>not even a Grog.</i>

05:56.980 --> 05:58.820
The final round?

06:00.070 --> 06:02.150
Mr. Rush, you must rest.

06:04.530 --> 06:06.120
I suppose you're right.

06:06.280 --> 06:09.120
But I just wanted
to cheer on the kids.

06:11.290 --> 06:15.330
We now call forth
the Earth team.

06:21.720 --> 06:22.720
How does she feel?

06:22.880 --> 06:25.760
The steering feels a bit stiff.
But I'll get used to it.

06:28.560 --> 06:34.140
Challenged by Toros,
colonel of the Crog lmperium.

06:58.630 --> 07:00.000
Mr. Rush!

07:05.720 --> 07:08.510
This is much better
than being in the hospital.

07:14.810 --> 07:16.270
Go Molly!

07:28.320 --> 07:29.490
Molly, what's wrong?

07:30.030 --> 07:33.240
It's a new star-racer.
Just let me get the hang of it.

07:36.920 --> 07:39.210
<i>Come on, Eva, this is it.</i>

07:39.380 --> 07:41.090
<i>I must do it.</i>

07:41.290 --> 07:42.630
<i>I have no choice.</i>

07:51.930 --> 07:53.390
<i>That's my girl.</i>

07:57.520 --> 07:58.850
Let's see what she's got.

08:06.610 --> 08:07.990
<i>Out of my way, Grog.</i>

08:20.580 --> 08:23.500
Give it to him, Jordan!
He deserves it!

08:31.510 --> 08:33.850
OK, I'm having
a bit of déjé vu back here.

08:36.640 --> 08:38.440
We need some speed, Molly!

08:48.740 --> 08:50.660
This has gone on long enough.

09:02.920 --> 09:03.840
Molly!

09:21.100 --> 09:22.730
I've learned my lesson, Toros.

09:22.900 --> 09:24.520
You can't trick me twice.

09:24.690 --> 09:26.900
Stan, the hyperdrive,
is it fixed?

09:27.070 --> 09:29.570
Roger that.
Same command as before.

09:48.840 --> 09:50.720
How can we achieve such speed?

09:51.010 --> 09:54.340
It was easy, really.
We mounted the turbines in clusters.

09:54.550 --> 09:55.390
That was my idea.

09:56.010 --> 09:57.430
It nearly doubles their capacity.

09:58.140 --> 10:01.390
-Fuel level?
-You're still OK for a bit longer.

10:01.640 --> 10:03.350
We've also increased
the tank capacity.

10:12.030 --> 10:13.780
How in the world
did that happen?

10:13.950 --> 10:15.910
Koji, can we make
this baby go faster?

10:17.740 --> 10:19.330
Well? Yes or no.

10:19.490 --> 10:20.620
Stan, what about the...

10:21.330 --> 10:22.790
Totally out of the question.

10:23.120 --> 10:25.420
The Arrow's hull could break apart
under the thrust.

10:31.970 --> 10:32.970
Hello!

10:33.550 --> 10:35.090
Toros is getting away!

10:36.340 --> 10:37.930
We haven't had
a chance to test it.

10:38.100 --> 10:39.640
It's just not safe yet.

10:42.180 --> 10:45.100
Stan, please do it.
We have no other choice.

10:45.520 --> 10:48.150
-But Don...
-I assume full responsibility.

10:49.480 --> 10:51.150
I do this under protest.

10:52.530 --> 10:54.240
Booster drives enabled.

11:13.840 --> 11:15.050
The hull is holding.

11:26.140 --> 11:27.150
By Kramm!

11:31.940 --> 11:33.780
-Come on!
-Go Molly, go!

11:33.940 --> 11:36.910
Win big so our fans
will love us again!

12:38.220 --> 12:39.380
Here goes nothing.

12:53.520 --> 12:56.280
You're going to crash
against the temple walls.

12:56.480 --> 12:58.240
You must stop now, Molly.

12:58.440 --> 13:00.110
I am not stopping.

13:00.780 --> 13:02.240
I know Maya wouldn't have.

13:05.790 --> 13:08.120
Foolish human.
You'll destroy us both.

13:13.080 --> 13:14.790
Molly, it's Rick.
Stop the booster drives.

13:14.960 --> 13:16.000
It's too risky.

13:31.600 --> 13:32.980
Molly, do it!

13:36.730 --> 13:38.360
I can't stop yet.

13:40.570 --> 13:41.530
No, Molly!

14:14.600 --> 14:16.060
Yeah, she did it!

14:18.320 --> 14:20.990
Not even I
could have pulled that stunt.

14:24.990 --> 14:27.660
The winner is the Earth team!

14:28.830 --> 14:29.620
We made it!

14:29.790 --> 14:31.700
I mean, they made it!

14:39.880 --> 14:41.840
<i>Torus has five victories,</i>

14:42.010 --> 14:45.090
and is therefore
qualified for Oban.

14:46.590 --> 14:49.430
The Earth team has
three victories,

14:49.600 --> 14:53.560
and must therefore wait
for the results of the competition

14:53.730 --> 14:56.190
between Prince Aikka and Spirit.

14:56.600 --> 14:59.320
But the humans just beat
the best racer.

14:59.480 --> 15:01.440
Surely they must
qualify for Oban.

15:05.070 --> 15:07.410
If Prince Aikka wins,
the Earth team

15:07.570 --> 15:09.450
will qualify for the finals.

15:09.660 --> 15:13.160
A victory for Spirit
would create a tie in his favor,

15:13.330 --> 15:16.830
and disqualify
the Earth team from Oban.

15:17.040 --> 15:19.130
You've got to be kidding me!

15:21.880 --> 15:23.710
Spirit has beaten us before.

15:23.970 --> 15:25.300
In the event of a tie,

15:25.470 --> 15:27.640
Spirit would have
the advantage over us.

15:27.800 --> 15:28.930
He would be the winner.

15:29.350 --> 15:32.100
It's all clearly spelled out
in these rules.

15:32.270 --> 15:33.470
We have to accept it.

15:40.980 --> 15:43.230
You know that Aikka
will lose this race on purpose,

15:43.400 --> 15:44.860
so the Crogs can win.

15:45.030 --> 15:46.400
Anyway, everybody knows

15:46.570 --> 15:48.450
the Nourasians are
in the Crog's pocket.

15:48.610 --> 15:50.700
Please don't start
with that again, Jordan.

15:50.870 --> 15:52.580
Believe whatever you want.

15:52.910 --> 15:54.450
But I saw them together.

15:54.620 --> 15:56.620
We now call forth

15:56.790 --> 16:00.380
Aikka, prince of Nourasia.

16:03.000 --> 16:05.420
<i>Molly, please,
don't look at me this way.</i>

16:05.590 --> 16:07.340
<i>It only makes it harder.</i>

16:09.680 --> 16:12.810
Challenged by Spirit,
Ambassador of the Phils.

16:13.390 --> 16:16.390
I hope you've made things clear
to your young master.

16:16.810 --> 16:18.690
Absolutely clear.

16:18.850 --> 16:22.400
The prince will do
as you have requested.

16:22.940 --> 16:25.030
I am pleased to hear this.

16:25.190 --> 16:26.990
Earth must be taught a lesson.

16:36.700 --> 16:37.870
Will you look at that?

16:38.040 --> 16:41.040
The honest prince is not even
pretending to race.

16:41.210 --> 16:42.670
It's impossible.

16:42.840 --> 16:44.750
Nourasian knights have honor.

16:44.920 --> 16:46.260
He won't let me down.

16:50.220 --> 16:51.430
G'dar, calm down.

16:51.590 --> 16:53.180
This is not our day for victory.

17:01.020 --> 17:02.860
I feel the same way.

17:03.020 --> 17:06.360
We are betraying
our friends and ourselves.

17:07.110 --> 17:08.530
This cannot continue.

17:09.070 --> 17:11.530
<i>Unsakai', G'dar wakhar!</i>

17:16.620 --> 17:18.750
What is this treachery?

17:18.910 --> 17:20.290
I... I don't know.

17:26.840 --> 17:29.840
You fight well, Spirit,
but today, I must win.

17:30.420 --> 17:32.760
<i>Unsakai', nourama safar!</i>

17:46.440 --> 17:48.110
Prince Aikka wins.

17:51.070 --> 17:55.530
The three teams selected
for the Grand Finals on Oban are...

17:56.370 --> 17:59.160
The Crogs, with five victories.

17:59.540 --> 18:02.580
The Nourasians, with four victories.

18:02.790 --> 18:06.590
And the Earth team,
with three victories.

18:11.670 --> 18:15.340
Failing the Crogs was
a most deadly mistake.

18:15.510 --> 18:18.010
This day will not be forgotten.

18:18.220 --> 18:19.350
Colonel, wait.

18:20.810 --> 18:22.730
You know, this guy's OK.

18:23.060 --> 18:25.940
And who knows,
I may even start to hate him less.

18:26.150 --> 18:26.900
Yeah!

18:31.490 --> 18:34.820
Rick, I haven't felt
this good in years,

18:34.990 --> 18:37.370
since you won
your first Earth Grand Prix.

18:37.530 --> 18:39.240
-You remember?
-Yeah.

18:39.990 --> 18:42.080
You can be proud of yourself, Rick.

18:42.250 --> 18:43.830
You certainly changed that girl.

18:44.460 --> 18:46.040
I couldn't have done it.

19:14.700 --> 19:16.240
Rick, can I come in?

19:17.490 --> 19:18.160
Rick?

19:33.510 --> 19:36.340
Have you guys seen Rick?
I can't find him anywhere.

19:36.510 --> 19:39.050
Yeah, I think he walked out
about a half an hour ago.

19:39.510 --> 19:40.720
He had his backpack with him.

19:42.220 --> 19:42.970
Thanks.

19:49.480 --> 19:51.440
Rick? Rick, where are you?

19:51.610 --> 19:53.070
Great race.

19:53.400 --> 19:55.320
You've changed so much, Molly.

19:55.490 --> 19:57.410
I can hardly recognize you.

19:57.570 --> 19:59.660
I'm looking for Rick.
Have you seen him?

19:59.820 --> 20:03.740
Rick? Well, yes I have.
He's heading back to Earth.

20:04.120 --> 20:07.250
-To Earth?
-He's right over there.

20:09.000 --> 20:09.750
Rick!

20:11.290 --> 20:15.090
These humans really are
fascinating creatures.

20:17.050 --> 20:18.510
Rick, wait!

20:19.680 --> 20:21.600
Rick, what are you doing?

20:21.760 --> 20:24.640
We're on our way to Oban.
You can't leave now.

20:24.810 --> 20:27.890
I've taught you everything I know,
little mouse. Racing's over for me.

20:28.940 --> 20:30.730
-But I...
-Ship's ready for takeoff!

20:30.900 --> 20:33.070
It's time for me
to think about my new life.

20:33.230 --> 20:34.980
You'll do just fine.

20:35.150 --> 20:35.990
Rick.

21:06.020 --> 21:07.810
Goodbye, Rick!

21:11.230 --> 21:12.860
And thank you for everything.

21:20.990 --> 21:22.490
Goodbye, champion.
